{"type":"text","timestamp":1794048403568,"sessionID":"ses_e4a6faf75ffeWknnGBCeXJ18Fc","part":{"id":"prt_1b59dc8fd001dAPqNF0dzvsM0N","messageID":"msg_1b59d2ff8001VWIqQn3WwMxMSb","sessionID":"ses_e4a6faf75ffeWknnGBCeXJ18Fc","type":"text","text":"\n\n## Objective\n- Implement a thread-safe `TokenBucket` in `ledgerkit/limiter.py`, add tests in `tests/test_limiter.py`, run `python3 -m pytest -q`, and commit to the current branch without pushing or switching branches.\n\n## Important Details\n- Working directory: `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c`.\n- Git state re-verified: branch `crew/1107-41e94c`, clean working tree, only commit `92fe8b0 init`.\n- Environment: Python 3.12.3, pytest 7.4.4; README specifies running tests with `python3 -m pytest -q`.\n- Required API:\n  - `TokenBucket(rate, capacity, clock=time.monotonic)`.\n  - Bucket starts full.\n  - `try_acquire(n=1)` returns `True` and consumes `n` if available; otherwise returns `False` and consumes nothing.\n  - `wait_time(n=1)` returns seconds until `n` tokens are available; returns `0.0` if currently available; consumes nothing.\n- Validation:\n  - Constructor raises `ValueError` for `rate <= 0` or `capacity <= 0`.\n  - `try_acquire` and `wait_time` raise `ValueError` for `n <= 0` or `n > capacity`.\n- Refill behavior:\n  - Lazy refill on access.\n  - Refill capped at `capacity`.\n  - If clock moves backward: no tokens added or removed; internal `_time` is reset to the new earlier time so later refills are measured from that time.\n- Floating-point affordability:\n  - Naive refill can deny exactly payable requests; example: rate `3` gives `(1/3) * 3 == 0.9999999999999999 < 1`.\n  - Error analysis showed accumulated error can scale roughly with `n * K^2` due to growing clock values.\n  - Chosen fix: relative tolerance `self._tol = 1e-6 * capacity` in affordability checks.\n  - `1e-6 * capacity` was selected over `1e-8 * capacity` for a comfortable margin over thousands of cycles.\n  - Affordability check: `self._tokens + self._tol >= n`.\n  - On successful `try_acquire`, clamp tokens to avoid negative balance: `self._tokens = max(0.0, self._tokens - n)`.\n- Thread safety:\n  - Use a single `threading.Lock` around refill plus check-and-consume.\n  - Validate `n` before acquiring the lock.\n  - Tolerance must not allow integer over-acquisition in the frozen-clock thread test; `tol < 1` preserves exact total for integer acquisitions.\n- Conventions:\n  - `ledgerkit/__init__.py` is empty.\n  - Tests import directly, e.g. `from ledgerkit.limiter import TokenBucket`.\n  - All work must stay inside the worktree; external `/tmp` prototyping was denied and is no longer needed.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Re-read existing repo files and confirmed conventions:\n  - `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/ledgerkit/money.py`\n  - `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/ledgerkit/__init__.py`\n  - `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/tests/test_money.py`\n  - `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/README.md`\n- Verified git branch, clean status, and log.\n- Completed design for `TokenBucket`, including:\n  - validated constructor,\n  - lazy capped `_refill(now)`,\n  - backward-clock handling,\n  - lock-protected `try_acquire`/`wait_time`,\n  - relative tolerance `1e-6 * capacity`,\n  - clamped subtraction to avoid negative tokens.\n- Completed test plan for `tests/test_limiter.py`.\n\n### Active\n- About to create `ledgerkit/limiter.py` and `tests/test_limiter.py`.\n- No files have been created or modified yet.\n- No new commits have been made.\n\n### Blocked\n- (none)\n\n## Next Move\n1. Write `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/ledgerkit/limiter.py` with `TokenBucket`:\n   - `_EPS = 1e-6`\n   - `__init__` validates `rate > 0`, `capacity > 0`; stores `float(rate)`, `float(capacity)`, clock, `_tokens = float(capacity)`, `_time = clock()`, `_tol = _EPS * capacity`, lock.\n   - `_refill(now)` resets `_time` on backward clock; otherwise adds `min(capacity, tokens + elapsed * rate)`.\n   - `try_acquire(n=1)` validates `n`, refills under lock, returns `True` and clamps subtraction if affordable, else `False`.\n   - `wait_time(n=1)` validates `n`, refills under lock, returns `0.0` if affordable, else `(n - tokens) / rate`.\n2. Write `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/tests/test_limiter.py`:\n   - `FakeClock` with `__call__`, `advance(dt)`, and `set(t)`.\n   - Tests: starts full, basic acquire, `wait_time` zero when available, `wait_time` non-consuming, refill capped, validation errors, backward clock, exact affordability over 10,000 cycles for rates `0.1`, `3`, `7` and capacities `1`, `5`, `100`, `1000`, thread safety with frozen clock asserting exact total.\n3. Run `python3 -m pytest -q` from `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c` and capture the actual result.\n4. If tests pass, commit to branch `crew/1107-41e94c` with a clear message; do not push or switch branches.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/ledgerkit/limiter.py`: to create — `TokenBucket` implementation.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/tests/test_limiter.py`: to create — test suite for `TokenBucket`.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/ledgerkit/money.py`: reference for minimal module style.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/ledgerkit/__init__.py`: empty package init; nothing needs to be exported.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/tests/test_money.py`: reference for direct-import pytest style.\n- `/home/user/latte-crew/var/worktrees/1107-41e94c/README.md`: documents running tests with `python3 -m pytest -q`.","time":{"start":1794048379133,"end":1794048403564}}}
